      <pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 07:26:16 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Props to the devs for spending almost 2 years trying to solve a bug that wasy even their fault. Just imagine that, 2 years! And they had to send Nvidia a PC for that to happen. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/after-a-year-and-a-half-of-rigorous-testing-path-of-exile-2-devs-finally-convinced-nvidia-to-fix-a-driver-bug-by-sending-it-an-entire-pc/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" translate="no"&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ellipsis"&gt;pcgamer.com/games/rpg/after-a-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;year-and-a-half-of-rigorous-testing-path-of-exile-2-devs-finally-convinced-nvidia-to-fix-a-driver-bug-by-sending-it-an-entire-pc/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://cdn.masto.host/mastodongamedevplace/media_attachments/files/117/019/061/495/692/143/original/8fa35c4195d0fc01.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" fileSize="96664" medium="image">
        <media:rating scheme="urn:simple">nonadult</media:rating>
        <media:description type="plain">After a year and a half of rigorous testing, Path of Exile 2 devs finally convinced Nvidia to fix a driver bug by sending it an entire PC</media:description>
      </media:content>
    </item>
    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117007986611412755</guid>
      <link>https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@djlink/117007986611412755</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 08:29:46 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;pretty cool, I think this is the tech companies should be embracing, but hard for them to profit on it. Need a thing? print it at home! most of friction still is finding models of a thing you need to print, especially for people who don&amp;#39;t know how to do the 3D models.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://cdn.masto.host/mastodongamedevplace/media_attachments/files/117/007/986/562/848/417/original/5d21f7f35e788ec9.png" type="image/png" fileSize="306640" medium="image">
        <media:rating scheme="urn:simple">nonadult</media:rating>
        <media:description type="plain"> Noctua and Prusa launch PETG filament for self-printed GPU coolers

Noctua and Prusa Research have released Prusament PETG filament in Noctua Beige and Noctua Brown. The material is intended for custom PC cases, electronic enclosures and air ducts, including user-designed GPU fan shrouds and cooling brackets.

</media:description>
      </media:content>
    </item>
